- Mode of delivery: Caesarean section may be associated with higher postpartum depression risk due to recovery complications.
- Newborn illness: Ill newborns can increase maternal stress and risk of depression.
- Number of household members: Larger households might provide more support or more stress, depending on dynamics; smaller households might mean less support.
- Education Level: Lower education levels might be associated with higher depression risk due to socioeconomic factors.

